And this seemed to him in his heart the best plan,
to send to Atreus’-son Agamemnon a ruinous Dream;
and, lifting his voice, to it winged words he spoke:

for she has bent them all,
Hera, entreating, and on the Trojans sorrows are fastened
from Zeus;

for she has bent them all,
Hera, entreating, and on the Trojans sorrows are fastened
from Zeus;

“O friends, leaders and lords of the Argives,
if some other of the Achaeans had told of the dream,
a falsehood we should call it and turn away from it all the more;
